Features of the Website

1. User Panel
View Cars for Rent: Display all available cars with details like price, description, availability, and images.
Book a Car: Users can select a car, provide their booking details, and submit a request.
Check Booking Status: Users can check whether their booking is approved or pending.

2. Admin Panel
Add Car: Admin can add new cars with details (e.g., name, model, price, description, image, availability).
Delete Car: Admin can remove cars from the inventory.
Approve Bookings: Admin can view user booking requests and approve or reject them.
Set Availability: Admin can set the dates when the car is available for rent.

3. Shared Features
Responsive design for mobile, tablet, and desktop views.
Authentication for user and admin roles.
Implementation Plan

1. Tech Stack
Frontend: HTML, CSS, JavaScript (React.js or plain JavaScript with Bootstrap for responsiveness)
Backend: Node.js with Express.js (or Django/PHP as alternatives)
Database: MongoDB or MySQL to store car details, bookings, and user information.
Authentication: JWT or session-based for user login and admin panel security.

2. Website Pages
User Panel
Home Page: Show available cars.
Car Details Page: Show detailed information about a car.
Booking Page: Allow users to submit booking requests.
Login/Signup Page: Authentication for users.
Admin Panel
Dashboard: Summary of bookings and cars.
Add Car: Form to add car details.
Manage Cars: List of cars with options to edit or delete.
Booking Requests: Approve or reject user bookings.

3. Database Schema
Cars Table
Field	Type	Description
id	Integer	Unique identifier
name	String	Car name
model	String	Car model/year
price	Decimal	Rental price per day
description	Text	Car description
image	String	Image URL
availability	DateRange	Dates car is available
Users Table
Field	Type	Description
id	Integer	Unique identifier
username	String	User's name
password	String	Password hash
Bookings Table
Field	Type	Description
id	Integer	Unique identifier
user_id	Foreign Key	ID of the user
car_id	Foreign Key	ID of the booked car
status	Enum	Pending/Approved
start_date	Date	Booking start date
end_date	Date	Booking end date

